SUMMARY:"Bracelets for Warriors" - Bracelet-Making Workshop focusing on Heart Health
DESCRIPTION:On Saturday August 29 at 10:30 AM\, we will host a 
 family-friendly bracelet-making workshop from Bracelets for Warriors\, led 
 by Joyce Cortez\, a rising senior this year at Paramus 
 Catholic.\n\nWhat’s included?\n\n\n	Create your own bracelet to take 
 home!\n	Learn simple\, age-appropriate heart health tips\n	Hear the 
 inspiring story behind Bracelets for Warriors\n\n\nThis program is ideal 
 for kids in grades 2-5\, but kids in grades K-1 may participate as well 
 with adult support.  \n\nSpace is limited to only 25 participants\;  
 registration is required!\n\nJoyce designed this community initiative after 
 her dad's open heart surgery.  Her goal is to educate youth and families 
 about the importance of heart health\, while offering a positive and 
 creative experience they will love.  Her presentation includes information 
 on what the heart does and how to introduce habits to keep your heart 
 healthy.\n\n
LOCATION:Nutley - Stockton Room
ORGANIZER;CN="Nutley Library":MAILTO:events@nutley.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Craft
