DTEND:20261002T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
SUMMARY:Library Speakers Consortium - Courage\, Choice\, and What Comes Next with Dystopian Icon Veronica Roth
DESCRIPTION:You must register here to attend:  
 https://libraryc.org/nutleypubliclibrary/212653\n\n\n\nA single choice can 
 transform your destiny. Join us for an online conversation with #1 New York 
 Times bestselling author Veronica Roth as we celebrate the enduring legacy 
 of her Divergent series\, one of the most iconic young adult series of a 
 generation\, and get an exclusive sneak peek into her highly anticipated 
 upcoming novel\, The Sixth Faction!\n\nFifteen years after readers first 
 stepped into dystopian Chicago alongside Tris Prior\, the Divergent 
 universe continues to captivate readers with its unflinching exploration of 
 identity\, courage\, and sacrifice. And in the alternate universe of The 
 Sixth Faction\, we revisit familiar characters in a completely new way… 
 \n\nBeatrice Prior stands on the brink of a decision every person in her 
 world must make: five factions\, five futures\, five lives.\n\nShe has a 
 plan: she’s going to make the bravest choice and leave Abnegation to join 
 Dauntless\, even though it means abandoning her family.\n\nBut when tragedy 
 strikes at her choosing ceremony\, everything changes—her world\, her 
 plans\, even Beatrice herself.\n\nHer decision will thrust her into the 
 crosshairs of an underground rebellion\, where a boy with secrets as 
 dangerous as her own—a boy with only a number for a name—may be the 
 only person she can trust.\n\nOne choice will change 
 everything.\n\nRegister now for the chance to ask questions and get an 
 exclusive sneak peek of The Sixth Faction–out on October 6\, 2026!\n\n 
 \n\nAbout the Author: \n\nVeronica Roth is the #1 New York Times 
 best-selling author of numerous titles including When Among Crows\, Chosen 
 Ones\, the Divergent series\, Carve the Mark\, and Seek the Traitor’s 
 Son. Veronica lives with her husband and their dog in Chicago\, a city that 
 she lovingly features (and frequently destroys) in many of her 
 novels.\n\n\n\n
LOCATION:Nutley Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Nutley Library":MAILTO:events@nutley.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Author Event/Talk
UID:LibCal-10315-17516277
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17516277
END:VEVENT
